  "details": "With the addition of mirrors in vrchat things became much easier but I have some suggestions that can make the user experience much better.\n.\nOne of the things I really liked was the mirror that was lock to the head when performing the fullbody traking calibration.\nI understand that a lot of people didn't like this function but it wouldn't hurt to keep it as a toggle for people who liked it.\n.\nAnother thing I would love to see is snaping for the mirror, I usually like to have the mirror perpendicular to the floor.\nit would be very useful to have a toggle to activate the snap at certain angles for example 90, 60, 30 and etc.\n.\nA option to change the default distance of the mirror when it Spawn it would be very good too, because I always need to adjust it to the distance I like.\n.\nhaving an option to recenter the mirror, similar to what XSOverlay has for windows would be great.\nsometimes when I'm chatting I tend to turn around a lot and when I noticed the mirror is already gone, then I need to Search for mirror to reposition or worse deactivate and activate, then I'll need to move it again at the distance and angle I like, so having an option to recenter would be really nice.\n.\nthese are some of the suggestions I have for the mirror, I would love to see them in the game, they would make the user experience much more satisfying.",
